<title>UK: RESEARCH ALERT-Sberbank started at CSFB.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT-Sberbank started at CSFB.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's Sberbank was rated &quot;buy&quot; as CS First Boston began coverage of the stock, the investment bank said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Analyst Andrei Arofikin said the bank, already Russia's largest, was growing even bigger because of customers' flight to quality in the restructuring banking sector.</p>
<p>He said Sberbank had a strategy designed to prepare for deregulation which implied building a competitive range of retail and corporate services by 2000, and set a target price of $257 by end 1997 provided it places new shares with non-residents.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
